   "reason": "DATA_GAP:shares \u2014 no diluted share count is carried in EDGAR companyfacts for any fiscal year (shares_diluted blank in financials_history.csv), so the engine emits no tier. The GAAP Class A diluted count in the 10-K EPS note (138,246,414 for FY2025) is NOT the right denominator for consolidated owner's earnings: Ryan is an Up-C \u2014 consolidated OCF/capex/SBC cover 100% of Ryan Specialty, LLC including the noncontrolling interest, while the GAAP diluted count excludes the 135,429,254 exchangeable LLC Common Units as antidilutive for FY2025 (they were dilutive and included in several 2025 quarters, e.g. Q3 2025 diluted 273,462k \u2014 the GAAP denominator flips with the antidilution test and cannot divide a consolidated numerator). The company's own adjusted diluted share count (279,029k for FY2025) is the total-economic-share denominator built for exactly this perimeter: Class A diluted + all LLC Common Units as exchanged + unvested award dilution. The engine applies this single FY2025 value to every missing year; FY2024's own adjusted count in the same release is 276,288k, so FY2024 OE/share is understated ~1.0% and FY2023 by a similar small amount \u2014 disclosed, small, and in the conservative direction for the median base year. The same value is the TTM denominator in ttm.json (H1 2026's own adjusted count was 270,080k after Q2 2026 buybacks, so the TTM base is ~3% conservative).",
